13:["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-[clamp(28px,3.6vw,44px)] font-black text-ink tracking-[-0.025em] leading-[1.05] font-sans","children":["Articles in Chapter ",1]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif text-ink-muted text-base mt-1","children":"Select an article to read its legal clauses and plain language meaning."}]]}],["$","$L21",null,{"articles":[{"articleNumber":1,"title":"Sovereignty of the people","summary":"All sovereign power belongs to the people of Kenya and shall be exercised only in accordance with this Constitution.","clauses":[{"clauseNumber":"(1)","text":"All sovereign power belongs to the people of Kenya and shall be exercised only in accordance with this Constitution."},{"clauseNumber":"(2)","text":"The people may exercise their sovereign power either directly or through their democratically elected representatives."},{"clauseNumber":"(3)","text":"Sovereign power under this Constitution is delegated to the following State organs, which shall perform their functions in accordance with this Constitution: (a) Parliament and the legislative assemblies in the county governments; (b) the national executive and the executive structures in the county governments; and (c) the Judiciary and independent tribunals."},{"clauseNumber":"(4)","text":"The sovereign power of the people is exercised at: (a) the national level; and (b) the county level."}],"plainExplanation":"Citizens hold the ultimate authority in Kenya. Leaders and State officers are caretakers delegated to serve under strict constitutional limits."},{"articleNumber":2,"title":"Supremacy of this Constitution","summary":"The Constitution is the supreme law of the Republic and invalidates any inconsistent law, customary practice, or executive action.","clauses":[{"clauseNumber":"(1)","text":"This Constitution is the supreme law of the Republic and binds all persons and all State organs at both levels of government."},{"clauseNumber":"(2)","text":"No person may claim or exercise State authority except as authorized under this Constitution."},{"clauseNumber":"(3)","text":"The validity or legality of this Constitution is not subject to challenge by or before any court or other State organ."},{"clauseNumber":"(4)","text":"Any law, including customary law, that is inconsistent with this Constitution is void to the extent of the inconsistency, and any act or omission in contravention of this Constitution is invalid."},{"clauseNumber":"(5)","text":"The general rules of international law shall form part of the law of Kenya."},{"clauseNumber":"(6)","text":"Any treaty or convention ratified by Kenya shall form part of the law of Kenya under this Constitution."}],"plainExplanation":"No president, parliament, governor, police officer, or customary tradition is above this document. Any illegal directive is unconstitutional and unenforceable."},{"articleNumber":3,"title":"Defense of this Constitution","summary":"Places a constitutional obligation on every person to protect, uphold, and resist any unlawful suspension or overthrow of the Constitution.","clauses":[{"clauseNumber":"(1)","text":"Every person has an obligation to respect, uphold and defend this Constitution."},{"clauseNumber":"(2)","text":"Any attempt to establish a government otherwise than in compliance with this Constitution is unlawful."}],"plainExplanation":"Defending the constitutional order is a legal right and a civic duty for every Kenyan citizen."}],"chapterNumber":1}]]}]
